                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is mildly decreased at 64 mL/min/1.73 m², indicating stage 2 chronic kidney disease. This is common in elderly patients and may reflect age-related decline. Recommend monitoring renal function and assessing for risk factors or comorbidities. No acute concern based on this isolated result.</td>
